# F-19: @Expr on a function parameter produces Annotation::Quote at parse time.
# The parser converts "@Expr" text to Annotation::Quote immediately, making it
# independent of any prelude type name. The function still evaluates normally
# (annotation-of on the function returns its extra annotation dict).
[
  # Function with @Expr annotated parameter — the annotation is Quote sentinel.
  f@[doc: "accepts expr"]: [fn [let x@Expr] x]
  # annotation-of the function returns the extra dict with doc field.
  ann: [annotation-of f]
  result: [= ann.doc "accepts expr"]
]
=== out
Dict({"f": Function(x), "ann": Dict({"doc": String("accepts expr")}), "result": Variant(Boolean.True, Null)})
